# A cancelled takeover no longer leaves the character in the game for good. A login of a character that is still
# connected disconnects the old client, marks the character isConnecting and attaches the new connection 1 s later
# (ProtocolGame::connect). When the new connection was closed in that second, connect() returned early and left
# isConnecting set; Player::sendPing() never removes a character that is connecting, so it stayed in the world
# without a client (attackable, holding its instance, counted online) until its owner logged in again. Found in the
# stress test (server/README.md "Stress test"): a reconnect storm left a character online for good; reproduced with a
# second login closed right after it was sent (still online 75 s later, where the no-pong kick removes it after 60 s).
# connect() now clears isConnecting before it gives up. Guard: tools/reattach_ping_patch_test.py (CI).
# Applies after 0001-0034.
--- a/src/protocolgame.cpp
+++ b/src/protocolgame.cpp
@@ -424,6 +424,11 @@
 	if (isConnectionExpired()) {
 		//ProtocolGame::release() has been called at this point and the Connection object
 		//no longer exists, so we return to prevent leakage of the Player.
+		// Chaos (patch 0035): the takeover is off, so the character is no longer waiting for this connection. Left
+		// set, isConnecting kept Player::sendPing() from ever removing the character: it stayed in the game without
+		// a client until its owner logged in again (a login that replaced a connected client and was closed within
+		// the 1 s before this call).
+		foundPlayer->isConnecting = false;
 		return;
 	}
 
